From a9f69c35373433269a3aafec9630b84556ede955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:22:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Podcasts in the brain: search, a show's feed and an episode's
 audio, every address through the network guard

GET /api/podcast/search asks Apple's free, keyless iTunes Search API for podcasts only; GET /api/podcast/feed reads a show's RSS to a
cap and gives the phone the show and its episodes (date, length, size, newest first); GET or HEAD /api/podcast/audio streams one
episode's audio with its size said and a Range passed on, refused past 600 MB. The page's security policy lets the phone fetch only
its own address, so these must come through the brain. Every address is someone else's, so every fetch goes through netguard's
guardedFetch: never a private, loopback or local address, and every redirect checked before it is followed.

index.ts (protected) changes by one import and one route line, after the arcade's passthrough and behind the owner's sign-in like
every other /api route: that is the only way the new route can be reached. The brain test is run from security.test.mjs, so the
protected package.json is not changed.

